1101W1: Verify the device is set to "Private Network".
1101 Windows -> 1101W1
1101W2: Verify "File and Printer Sharing" is enabled.
1101W1 -> 1101W2
1101W3: Can you ping the device by hostname "ping (hostname)"?
1101W2 -> 1101W3
1101W4: On target PC open Command Prompt and run "ipconfig". Take note of the IPv4 Address. Run "hostname". Take note of the hostname. Run "ping (hostname) -4" and note the IP address. Does this match the first IP Address Noted?
1101W3 -> 1101W4:No
1101W5: In Command Prompt run "ipconfig /flushdns". If target goes offline wait until network restarts. If network never comes back up reboot target PC. Repeat last diagnostic step. Does "ipconfig" IP address now match IP address seen when using ping command?
1101W4 -> 1101W5: No
1101W6: Issue Resolved- DNS Resolver Cache was Corrupted on target PC. Cleaning the local DNS cache restored connection.
1101W5 -> 1101W6: Yes
1101W7: The DNS cache is corrupt on the router. Altering router data to resolve the root of the issue is outside of our scope of work.
1101W8: Set the device to use the IP Address of the target and inform end user connection may fail in future unless root issue is resolved or if IP Reservation is placed on Network.
1101W5 -> 1101W7: No
1101W7 -> 1101W8
1101W9: In Command Prompt attempt to ping the device by hostname using mDNS "ping (hostname).local". Does pinging the hostname now work?
1101W4 -> 1101W9: Yes
1101W10: Hostname remains unable to be resolved due to unidentifyable reason either with customer network or customer PC.
1101W9 -> 1101W10: No
1101W10 -> 1101W8
1101W11: Router is unable to resolve hostnames correctly. You are able to resolve the hostname by using mDNS resolution which is a DNS broadcast that bypasses DNS. MFPs do not support mDNS so appending .local to the Hostname in the MFP will not resolve the issue. Altering router data to resolve the root of the issue is outside of our scope of work.
1101W9 -> 1101W11: Yes
1101W11 -> 1101W8
1101W12: On target PC open Command Prompt and run "net share". Do you see a scan folder listed?
1101W3 -> 1101W12: Yes
1101W13: Issue Resolved- No Scan folder exists on PC. Create and share out a scan folder.
1101W12 -> 1101W13: No
1101W14: Attempt to connect to Network Share off another PC. Are you able to read and write to the scan folder?
1101W12 -> 1101W14: Yes
1101W15: Issue Resolved- Target PC either has issue outside our scope of work to resolve or has smb blocked by Firewall. Report findings to end user and discuss alternatives.
1101W14 -> 1101W15: No
1101W16: Is the device one of the following models? TASKalfa 3050ci - TASKalfa 3550ci - TASKalfa 4550ci - TASKalfa 5550ci - TASKalfa 1800 - TASKalfa 2200 - FS-1220MFP - FS-1320MFP - FS-1325MFP - FS-6025MFP - FS-6030MFP - FS-6525MFP - FS-6530MFP - FS-C8020MFP - FS-C8025MFP - FS-C8520MFP - FS-C8525MFP.
1101W14 -> 1101W16: Yes
1101W17: Legacy SMB (SMB 1.0) is not Supported on this model Kyocera.
1101W18: Inform End User this is disabled by default due to a known Security Exploit (WannaCry). Inform end user this legacy service can be enabled to allow scanning, but we are not liable if issues occur as a result.
1101W19: Search for "Turn Windows Features on or off" Scroll Down and open the dropdown for "SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support" Check both "SMB1.0/CIFS Client" and "SMB1.0/CIFS Server". Uncheck "SMB1.0/CIFS Automatic Removal". Apply the setting and restart if necessary.
1101W20: Issue Resolved- Kyocera MFP does not support SMB2.0 or SMB 3.0 for modern Windows versions.
1101W16 -> 1101W17: Yes
1101W17 -> 1101W18
1101W18 -> 1101W19: Enable legacy SMB (SMB1.0).
1101W18 -> 1101W20: Leave legacy SMB (SMB1.0) disabled.
1101W19 -> 1101W20
1101W21: If the port number on the destination is set to 445, set port to 139. If the port number is set to 139, set port to 445. Does SMB work now?
1101W16 -> 1101W21: No
1101W22: Issue Resolved- Target PC does not listen to either port 139 or 445.
1101W21 -> 1101W22: Yes
1101W23: Make a full device backup and then initialize the unit. Upon connecting back to network attempt to send another scan. Does SMB work now?
1101W21 -> 1101W23: No
1101W24: Issue Resolved- Unidentified bug in unit that was resolved with initialization.
1101W25: Unable to resolve source of issue. Consult with end user about alternatives.
1101W23 -> 1101W24: Yes
1101W23 -> 1101W25: No

