1102 -> 1102 Linux
1102W2: If is the device using a end user for the username or a scanner account?
1102 Windows -> 1102W2
1102W3: On target PC open Command Prompt and run "net user (username)". Is there a date next to "Password Expires:"?
1102W2 -> 1102W3: Scanner Account
1102W4: On target PC open Command Prompt and run "lusrmgr.msc" Do you recieve an error saying "This snap-in may not be used with this edition of Windows"
1102W3 -> 1102W4: Yes
1102W5: Issue Resolved- Click on Users and then right click on the scanner account and click properties. Check the box that says "Password Never Expires" and Apply settings.
1102W4 -> 1102W5: No
1102W6: On the target PC open Command Prompt and run "wmic". Does it return an error saying "'wmic' is not recognized as an internal or external command, operable program, or batch file."?
1102W4 -> 1102W6: Yes
1102W7: Issue Resolved- This PC is incompatible with any built-in utilities to disable password expiration for the scanner user account. Delete the scanner account and remake it within Windows settings and reshare out the folder with the newly created scanner account.
1102W6 -> 1102W7: Yes
1102W8: Issue Resolved- On target PC run 'wmic useraccount where Name="(username)" set PasswordExpires=false'. The account password has expired for the scanner account. This command will perminantly disable the password expiration for it.
1102W6 -> 1102W8: No
1102W9: Have end user reenter their password into address book. Does SMB work now?
1102W2 -> 1102W9: End user account
1102W10: Issue Resolved- End user changed account password
1102W9 -> 1102W10: Yes
1102W11: Unable to resolve source of authentication issue. Create a scanner account on target pc and attempt setup again.
1102W9 -> 1102W11: No

1103 -> 1103 Windows
1103 -> 1103 MACOS
1103 -> 1103 Linux
1103W2: Issue Resolved- user account doesn't have full read/write permissions to the specified network share. Go to the scan folder and right click and select "Properties". Go to the "Sharing" and under both locations add the user account to the share with "Full Control" Permissions.
1103 Windows -> 1103W2
1103L2: Issue Resolved- user account doesn't have full read/write permissions to the specified network share. Open a terminal window on the target device and run "sudo nano /etc/samba/smb.conf" and authenticate as a valid sudoer. Scroll down to the network share and create or append the user account as a valid user on a new line. This should look like "valid users=(username)". Press Ctrl+O to save changes. Press Ctrl+X to exit nano.
1103 Linux -> 1103L2

1105F: Issue Resolved- SMB Client is disabled on MFP. Authenticate into Command Center RX (Web Interface) Go to "Network Settings". Go to "Protocol". Underneath "Send Protocols", enable "SMB".
1105 -> 1105F

